WEBVTT

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.650
There are no classes today, on the 
day before the school festival.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.850
To prepare for tomorrow's battle,

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:15.910
we, the student council, 
will make the final preparations!

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:19.510
The success or failure of the school festival

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:22.650
is riding on the work you do right now!

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.650
Masaya-senpai seems more excited than usual.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.420
He seems to be really excited 
for the school festival,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.710
but could there be something else?

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:28.940
Let's do this!

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.700
Now, for a word from
the student council president!

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.200
We're at the final hurdle.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.460
We'll thoroughly check to see

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.250
that everyone is ready to ensure a 
perfect festival and after party...

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.430
Itsuki-kun.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.840
Sorry.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.990
Vice president, you're slacking!

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.760
Allow me to apologize for him.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:59.490
It's partly my fault for not letting 
Itsuki get any sleep last night.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:01.910
How bold.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.240
D-Do you mean...

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.010
Relations...

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:05.480
...of the sexual kind?

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.800
I-It's not like that!

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.750
We were preparing for the school festival!

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.080
Right, Aika?

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:12.890
Yes.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:13.840
"Aika"?

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:19.510
When did you two get on a first-name basis?

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.260
Please don't read too much into it!

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.520
In any case, let's make 
the festival a success.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.240
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.490
<b>Quest 10     Vessel</b>

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:07.330
They're gathering.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.080
Let's throw a wrench in their plans.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.940
It's already lunch. Where did they go?

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.340
Izumi-senpai.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.860
Do you have a minute?

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.210
Can Ai-Ai come help us today?

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:27.420
Ai-Ai?

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.300
She means Suzuki-san.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.900
Her name's Aika, so we call her Ai-Ai.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.600
She didn't go to class?

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.190
Not yet today.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:37.820
Lately she's been disappearing 
with Tachibana a lot.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.490
I see.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:43.060
I'll tell them to help with your class.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:45.370
Thanks.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.450
Senpai.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.800
Where have you been? Lunch is almost over.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.880
Sorry. I'll do it right away.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.130
We were visiting our class.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.130
There's work to be done there, too.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:06.540
Really?

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.770
Your classmates were looking 
for you, Suzuki-san.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:11.120
Understood.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:13.040
I'll head back to class.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:19.980
Um...

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:23.720
I don't need your excuses. 
Just finish your work, Tachibana-kun.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.030
Okay.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.590
The school festival is tomorrow. 
Let's do our best.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.290
Okay.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.730
Ai-Ai.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.300
Try this on.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.620
It was finished just this morning.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:45.430
It's your costume for tomorrow.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.470
We'll have to make some adjustments.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.180
Is this right?

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.380
Look. I told you the ribbon would be cute.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:05:00.940
We should have Ai-Ai in the center 
so she can be our poster girl.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.910
Center poster?

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:08.060
In other words, you'll handle the floor
and be our main fighting force.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:08.950
I see.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.770
In that case,

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.950
we must be using a crane wing
or spindle formation.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.830
M-Maybe, I guess.

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:20.360
The crêpe mix is here.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:20.960
Thanks.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:21.710
Hey, thanks.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:25.150
Hey, Kayano. This is the waitress costume.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:31.240
An angel has descended upon Seiga!

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:32.970
The perfect maid!

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:36.400
Looks like Ai-Ai should be the center.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.280
Yeah.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.980
I see. So this is my mission.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.060
Suzuki-san...

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:55.930
Do you have a minute?

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:02.340
Tachibana-kun seems to be
really tired lately.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.400
That's my fault.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.720
So you two are...

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:10.470
I'm sorry.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.920
You don't need to apologize.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:14.940
You're free to do what you want.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.540
I believe I understand
the two of you's circumstances.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:19.910
Our circumstances?

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:21.610
Did Itsuki tell you?

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.360
He didn't have to. I can tell.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.830
You're incredibly perceptive.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.060
So, since when?

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.870
Last Saturday.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:34.500
Saturday...

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.620
The day he skipped the meeting?

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.100
Did he skip to confess?

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:42.920
It was sudden.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:45.600
Apparently Itsuki didn't realize it himself.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:51.140
<i>He's always secretly had 
feelings for Suzuki-san?</i>

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:55.400
Itsuki is doing his best not 
to inconvenience others.

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:59.950
Sorry to say this, but I'd like you
to keep your distance.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:07.900
Suzuki-san.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:12.040
He tends to try to handle things on his own.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:15.780
Take good care of Tachibana-kun.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:17.660
I know.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:20.540
I will protect Itsuki with my life.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:41.280
That wore me out.

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.320
I finished.

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.320
Tachibana

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:56.330
He's pushing himself too hard.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:16.970
Itsuki, you there?

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.460
Are you asleep?

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:36.950
Itsuki.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:42.340
<i>Tachibana Itsuki-kun, 
I'm grateful for your help.</i>

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:44.620
Sure. This is for the best, right?

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:45.690
Yes.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.000
<i>Given that you're a suitable vessel,</i>

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.710
<i>you wouldn't have been 
able to avoid fighting,</i>

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:54.720
<i>and by fighting, you'll be 
able to save other Earthlings.</i>

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:01.520
<i>Of course, the ARKS will also 
offer all the support we can.</i>

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.860
But at this rate...

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:07.110
It's fine, Aika. I chose this.

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.270
<i>The second wave will be coming soon.</i>

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:13.460
<i>I've called for backup.</i>

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:15.200
<i>Try to hold on until then.</i>

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.540
A new boosted enemy?

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.120
I know.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:45.020
I will protect Itsuki with my life.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:49.750
<i>What's wrong with me?</i>

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:53.680
Why am I letting it bother me?

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:17.010
Itsuki!

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.000
Over here!

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:38.150
Sorry. I let my guard down.

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:39.820
Don't worry about it.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.910
You're just doing what you're supposed to do.

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:44.410
Protecting you is my duty.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.910
You should do your duty, too.

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:48.100
My duty?

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:49.000
They're coming.

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:52.010
Clarissa!

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:07.640
What was that?

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:10.400
That was close, Aika-chan.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.900
You're the backup 
the commander mentioned...

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:18.810
Matoi-sama?

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:21.780
Just call me Matoi.

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:23.780
Matoi-sama?

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:27.480
She's special to all of us ARKS.

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:30.290
I'm not that important.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:34.290
Anyway, are you okay?

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:36.290
What? Me?

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.220
I wonder why.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:41.650
You seem accustomed to battle,

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:44.280
so why are you so unaccustomed 
to using Photon Arts?

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:45.900
I-I...

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.060
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:50.700
Let me handle this.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:53.120
You two can retreat and rest.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:02.860
<b>[The Council of Six]</b>
The leaders, and possibly symbols,
of Arks everywhere. Numbers 1, 3, and 5 form the "Legendary Three Heroes,"
whereas 2, 4, and 6 are called "The Even Numbers." Including number 0, the seven of them possess exceptional fighting strength.
In the year A.P.240, more than half of them are on a special mission away from the fleet.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:07.870
<b>[Matoi]</b> Was once consumed by the dark as the vessel for the Profound Darkness,
but miraculously returned alive with the help of many people.
Currently operates as a Guardian,
one of the most special beings among ARKS.
Wields the Genesis weapon 
Clarissa Gen. 3.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:11.760
Tachibana-kun, today is the first day
of the school festival.

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:13.120
You're the vice president.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:18.160
You should have the spirit to 
show up before everyone else!

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:21.660
Masaya-senpai, your hype levels...

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:23.630
They're maxed out!

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:25.650
Behold this glorious weather!

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:28.890
<b>Seiga Academy
School Festival
2027</b>

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:27.810
It's the perfect day for a school festival!

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:35.600
He's so hyper...

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:36.900
...it's repulsive.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:43.060
Apparently someone Masaya-senpai admires 
is coming to the school festival today.

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:45.730
It's someone he met on <i>PSO2</i>.

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:46.160
Masayan

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:46.160
Finally going to meet my Cats-chan!!

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:49.420
Mika-san, have you been stalking
Masaya-senpai on social media?

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:51.610
I had to. He was acting too creepy.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:54.280
They've agreed to meet 
at the school festival.

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:55.070
So he's just...

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:56.050
...an idiot.

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:57.290
Wait a minute...

00:12:57.890 --> 00:13:01.300
I have a friend who refuses to meet me IRL,
no matter how much I invite them.

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:06.100
<i>Could it be?</i>

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:09.330
Either way,

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:13.690
you might be the reason Masaya-senpai 
is in such good spirits.

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:14.800
Yeah.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:17.690
You should wait to say that 
until after it's over.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.080
What? Don't get ahead of yourself.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:21.440
Tachibana-kun.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:23.520
Don't worry about us today.

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:25.070
You should help your class.

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:26.920
Okay.

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.320
Let us...

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:30.080
...handle the rest.

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:32.290
Thanks.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:40.340
Itsuki, can you draw in customers
and handle odd jobs?

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.050
We've already assigned
all the jobs inside the café.

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.090
Got it.

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:47.690
Is something wrong?

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:52.330
I've been tasked with leading 
the vanguard in this costume.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:53.670
What's she talking about?

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:57.590
Apparently it means she's been asked to
handle the center of the store as floor chief.

00:13:57.590 --> 00:13:58.600
I see.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:05.110
<i>The student council has an 
announcement for all students.</i>

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:10.120
<i>This year's Seiga Academy
school festival will now begin.</i>

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:13.620
<i>Please head to your stations.</i>

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:19.360
Today and tomorrow, let's do our very best to
make this the best school festival possible.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:29.890
Okay.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:33.890
Welcome to Seiga Academy!

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:36.890
Please enjoy the festival.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:39.320
We have wonderful cafés.

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:40.500
We have... have...

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:42.150
What?

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:48.400
Um, are you...

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:52.660
Are you Orga-Cats-chan?

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.910
No, I'm not.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:55.790
Then are you—

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:56.660
Hitsugi-chan!

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:59.580
This must be some new way to hit on people.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:00.810
Let's go.

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:04.040
Okay, okay. Excuse us.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.670
Hey, didn't our company make this?

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:10.100
Only you can weld like that.

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:12.680
You're starting to understand.

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:16.570
Are you Orga-Cats-chan?

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:18.810
No, I'm not.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.940
Gross!

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:28.360
We're grateful for the help 
from our sister school.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:31.360
Thank you for inviting us today.

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:33.990
I bought some.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.330
Have as much of whatever you'd like.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:39.220
What did you get?

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:41.090
I'm glad you asked.

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:44.870
Okonomiyaki, modanyaki, takoyaki, 
waffles, and mini castella.

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.850
It's all starchy stuff.

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:49.620
More importantly, let's go 
look for Itsuki's class.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.010
<b>Welcome Back,
Master ♥</b>

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:52.860
Nice, nice.

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:54.350
Last Samurai-san.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.300
We're here, Itsuki-kun.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:57.890
Tachibana's friends?

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.240
Probably from <i>PSO2</i>.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:15:59.890
Yeah, probably.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:03.780
Welcome back, master.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:05.810
M-Master.

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:10.150
Nice, nice. Your awkwardness is irresistible.

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:13.290
Um, Last Samurai-san...

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.340
Maybe we should try this at our inn.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:19.080
But I guess my wife can't compare 
with real-life 17 year olds.

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:20.830
Darling...

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:25.750
Uppercut!

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:32.090
I'll have some tea.

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:35.110
He's exactly the high school student
we imagined, isn't he?

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:37.860
How long are you going to 
keep being nervous, dude?

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:40.940
Did you skip breakfast?

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:44.180
I recommend vegetables. Organic ones.

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:48.520
Oh, yeah. The "Orga" in 
Orga-Cats is for organic.

00:16:57.550 --> 00:17:00.000
See you later, master.

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:02.100
They're so bright.

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:04.210
It's too much. See you later.

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:06.650
Is something wrong?

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:08.300
Something just—

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:11.210
Itsuki. Sorry, but could you
go throw out the trash?

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:13.090
Sure.

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:18.620
Aika-chan, how are you?

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:20.040
Tired?

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:21.280
I'm fine.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:22.720
I see.

00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:24.720
But the customers are starting to dwindle.

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:25.850
Why don't you take a break?

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:26.990
No, I'm fine.

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:28.280
Was it my imagination?

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:37.100
President, we're fine.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:40.640
We'd like to take a look around now.

00:17:41.130 --> 00:17:43.900
Besides, Kori seems to be at her limit.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:48.700
I see. Excuse me, then.

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.880
Where do you want to go?

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:02.700
What's wrong?

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:04.260
Why now?

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:05.330
Ai-Ai?

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:06.310
What is it?

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:08.320
I'm going to go check it out.

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:10.940
Kayano, too?

00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:14.100
Tachibana-kun, I'll help.

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:16.380
Senpai? Thanks.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:18.380
How's your class doing?

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:21.160
Thankfully, we're doing well.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:21.830
Really?

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.730
Well, you might as well enjoy yourself, too.

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:26.220
With Suzuki-san.

00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:28.830
Please stop joking about that.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:32.750
Aren't you dating?

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.380
Not you too!

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:36.590
I'm not dating Suzuki-san.

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:39.130
What? Really?

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:43.670
But she said she'd protect you.

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:44.360
What?

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:50.600
She was probably referring to how she's helping me out a lot in <i>PSO2</i>.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:53.360
She tends to get tongue-tied
and leave out crucial information.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:00.780
R-Right. She does tend to do that.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:01.660
Yeah.

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:06.430
The festival seems livelier than last year.

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:08.370
Yeah, it does.

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:12.000
This must be the kind of
school festival you wanted to see.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:12.920
What?

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.660
But there's still tomorrow.

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:20.870
It's still the school festival 
until the after party.

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:22.440
You're right.

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:27.730
It's because you and the rest of 
the student council worked so hard.

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:29.280
No, it's not like that.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:31.410
There's no need to be modest.

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:32.020
What?

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:35.020
I'm the one who chose you.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:38.320
Um...

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:43.160
Why did you choose me
 to be the vice president?

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:47.160
Because...

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:56.150
What is this?

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:57.960
Run away, Rina-senpai!

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:02.800
Tachibana-kun!

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:12.190
Run... quickly...

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:13.690
What's going on?

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:15.190
No!

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:22.700
Stop!

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:33.790
Rina-senpai?

00:20:35.590 --> 00:20:38.920
What is this? What's going on?

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:55.650
Could it be?

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:01.600
Does Rina have an affinity for Photons, too?

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:09.270
This isn't good.

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:15.970
Senpai!

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:27.540
Aika-chan.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:32.700
The Monomate girl?

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:35.850
Itsuki?

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:37.980
And Izumi-senpai?

00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:40.360
What is this?

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:48.360
Rina-senpai!

00:22:05.140 --> 00:22:06.330
No...

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:42.900
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:42.900 --> 00:24:10.300
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:43.790 --> 00:23:45.160
I'm satisfied.

00:23:45.160 --> 00:23:46.740
We've visited all the shops now.

00:23:46.740 --> 00:23:49.340
I don't think we had to do that.

00:23:49.340 --> 00:23:52.500
But it's my job as a member of the 
Tensei Academy student council.

00:23:52.500 --> 00:23:55.060
Really? Why don't you report on it, then?

00:23:55.060 --> 00:23:57.560
Uh, um... The takoyaki 
were fluffy and delicious.

00:23:57.560 --> 00:23:59.310
The crêpes were sweet and delicious, as well.

00:23:59.310 --> 00:24:02.510
And the maid café's uniforms 
were impressively made.

00:24:02.510 --> 00:24:05.290
Kori, why did you even come here?

00:24:05.290 --> 00:24:07.060
To hang out with you, Hitsugi-chan.

00:24:07.060 --> 00:24:07.940
Goodbye.

00:24:07.940 --> 00:24:10.760
I'm kidding! I'm kidding, Hitsugi-chan!
